\ Test per-operation native fallback for non-numeric types in compiled
\ words. Compiled comparison words receive different type combinations;
\ the per-op fallback calls the polymorphic native for operations that
\ the compiled fast path cannot handle.
\
\ In AOT mode bail is fatal, so correct output from every call proves
\ that per-op fallback handled each type combination without
\ re-executing the entire word through the interpreter.

add: ( a b -- c ) [ + ] ;
eq:  ( a b -- ? ) [ = ] ;
lt:  ( a b -- ? ) [ < ] ;

\ === Fixnum arithmetic (compiled fast path) ===
3 4 add .
10 3 add .

\ === Float arithmetic (compiled fast path) ===
1.5 2.5 add .

\ === Mixed fixnum/float (compiled polymorphic path) ===
3 2.5 add .
2.5 3 add .

\ === Comparison: fixnum via resolver (per-op native fallback) ===
5 5 eq .
3 5 eq .
3 5 lt .
5 3 lt .

\ === Comparison: string (per-op native fallback) ===
"abc" "abc" eq .
"abc" "xyz" eq .

\ === Comparison: type values (per-op native fallback) ===
fixnum fixnum eq .
fixnum float eq .

\ === Comparison: boolean (per-op native fallback) ===
t t eq .
t f eq .
